  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual mnemonic as the intended recipient of the absurd memory aid",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the text 'how to remember kid in hot car keep 2nd road beer with them!' as the person who is supposed to remember the safety rule. The meme's structure implies that the viewer (user) is the one who needs to recall the mnemonic, making the text the focal point of the user's projection. The user is not explicitly addressed with 'you' or 'me', but the imperative nature of the text ('how to remember') and the instructional framing project the user as the one who must apply this (illogical) mnemonic.",
